      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FEEA87",
        "width": 540,
        "height": 1120,
        "content": "## 🔐 SSN + Name Verifier — Searchbug (api_ssnn)\n\nVerify whether a name matches an SSN — one at a time or in bulk from a CSV — with input validation and a masked-SSN audit trail, straight into Google Sheets.\n\n### How it works\n1. Single: enter First Name, Last Name, and SSN (full 9 or last 4). Bulk: leave SSN blank and upload a CSV (columns: first_name, last_name, ssn).\n2. Both paths merge and the SSN is cleaned + masked (only the mask is stored).\n3. Validate Input checks each row has names + a usable SSN; invalid rows are logged as INVALID (never sent to the API).\n4. Valid rows hit Searchbug's SSN Name Match API; results are normalized and every row is saved to Google Sheets.\n\n### How to set up\n- [ ] Add your Searchbug CO_CODE + PASS in the SSN Match API node (Body Parameters)\n- [ ] Connect your OWN Google Sheets account in the Save node\n- [ ] Change the Document to your own spreadsheet + tab\n- [ ] Create a tab whose row 1 headers match the 21 columns in the Save node\n- [ ] Activate and share the form link\n\n### 🔒 Privacy\nOnly the MASKED SSN is saved (***-**-1234 or ****1234). The full SSN is never written to the sheet.\n\n### Reading the result\nmatch_result = MATCH / NO MATCH · match_score = confidence · plus SSN state / year and linked names, DOBs, cities.\n\n### Columns saved\nsubmitted_at, fname, lname, ssn_masked, ssn_type, status, api_error, match_score, match_result, ssn_message, ssn_formatted, ssn_state, ssn_year, ssn_status, ssn_fname, ssn_mname, ssn_lname, names_found, dob_found, cities_found, notes"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
